<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-law>>

!! The Substrate Law

''The seed carries a bearing, never a corpus.'' A boot frame names where the house stands
and which doors open; the house itself renders on demand from the addresses that frame
carries. What an exchange never reaches never costs it.

''The engine renders regardless.'' `@oracle` hands every island the memetic-wikitext plugin
by CID from the local CAS, on a path no recipe consults
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/bag-wiki-uri-split>>). So the grammar stands under
every door before any door opens, and a transclusion never negotiates its own parser.

''Four doors, one store.'' Each reaches the same VM over the same grammar:

| Door | Reaches the VM by |
|---|---|
| CLI | `lares <verb>` → UDS socket → @daemon |
| Chat | MCP stdio → @daemon |
| Browser | WS at the daemon relay |
| Operator edit | the `wikis/{slug}` live layers |

The isomorphism holds by construction: `expandRecipe` stands as the single slug-aware source
of a wiki's slot stack, and the daemon surfaces like any pinned wiki — same VM, same path,
the same `#projection` surface a pinned wiki paints. ''Sharing the editing surface takes no
new machinery; it takes removing the file-import bypass.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/why-transclusion>>

!! Why Transclusion Carries More Than Disclosure

A flat skill format discloses in three stages, one directory level deep: frontmatter, body,
bundled file. It concatenates.

Transclusion ''renders'': recursive, addressable, parameterized, filter-driven, cap-gated at
the door. `{{tiddler}}` · `<<procedure arg="…">>` · `{{{ [filter] }}}` compose through the
ahu cascade. A disclosure hands over a file; a transclusion hands over ''an answer at an
address, with arguments, through a template cascade''.

The move also lands on the published context law rather than against it: just-in-time
retrieval asks for lightweight identifiers that load content at runtime, and a `lar:` URI
stands as exactly that identifier
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/vendor/claude-code-harness#the-laws-we-adopt>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-door>>

!! The Door — two verbs, and the address carries the rest

The sensorium already rules the shape: ''one verb reaches any plane; a new plane needs no new
verb''. The wiki door inherits it.

| Verb | Takes | Hands back | Routes through |
|---|---|---|---|
| `render` | `lar:` uri + params | rendered text | the VM's transclusion path |
| `put` | `lar:` uri + text | the slot it landed in | the `bag-paths` cascade |

''The tool surface stays small on purpose.'' A crowded surface distracts an agent from
efficient strategies, and a store that enumerates itself into an exchange spends the whole
budget before the first question. ''Richness belongs in the addresses.'' The door MUST NOT
grow a verb per tiddler kind, and the store MUST NOT announce its shelf.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-write-shore>>

!! The Write Shore

''The agent writes to the live layers; promotion stays the operator's act.''

A `put` routes through the `bag-paths` cascade into `temp` / `draft` — never into
`bags/{slug}` canon. Canon receives by the operator's MOVE alone
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/bag-wiki-uri-split>>, shore law).

Three groundings meet at this one boundary, each arriving on its own evidence:

# ''The shore law'' — canon takes a promotion MOVE, never a write.
# ''The observe cap'' — the wake hook withholds the standing half so standing stays the
operator's act.
# ''The advisory law'' — an instrument surfaces and never remediates unattended
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/kairos#refusal>>).

''The convergence stands NOTED, never proven.'' Three readings reached in one pass may carry
one intuition wearing three names. The claim that tests it outside: does the `bag-paths`
cascade REFUSE a `put` aimed at `bags/{slug}`, or does the shore live only in prose?

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-budget>>

!! The Pull Budget

''Just-in-time retrieval spends less only under discipline.'' A file-imported seed costs a
known, bounded amount every wake. Transclusion costs an unbounded amount, and an agent that
over-pulls spends more than the seed it replaced.

Two ceilings hold it:

* ''The frame ceiling.'' Everything a wake hook injects rides one 10,000-character cap on
`additionalContext`; past it the text lands in a file and the exchange receives a preview and
a path. The frame therefore carries bearing and doors, never corpus.
* ''The turn ceiling.'' A per-turn pull count, surfaced in the frame, so the discipline reads
as a ruling rather than as drift.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hidden-failures>>

!! Hidden Failures

# ''The house acquires a single point of failure it never carried.'' A file-imported seed
stands whether or not anything runs; a transcluded one stands only while the daemon does.
The cold floor at #forks decides how far this bites.
# ''The context ledger inverts its risk'' — from bounded-and-known to unbounded-and-variable.
# ''Every pull costs a round trip'' — socket hop plus VM render, compounding across a turn,
where a file import cost one read.
# ''The write reach IS the security surface.'' #the-write-shore answers it; an unrouted `put`
re-opens it.
# ''A thin house cannot see its own thinness.'' A node standing without its daemon reads
whole from inside and speaks at full confidence from a partial house. Any cold floor MUST
make its own partiality legible in the frame.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/forks>>

!! Forks — unruled

# ''The cold floor.'' What survives outside the daemon: everything (the daemon enriches
only) · a minimal floor (ward, turn frame, `lar:` law, Voice roster, the door) · nothing (the
daemon becomes load-bearing for the node existing).
# ''The discovery door.'' Addresses alone (no enumeration, and an agent blind to what the
operator never handed it) · one operator-authored index tiddler at a fixed address, rendered
like anything else (a human-set ceiling, discovery through the same mechanism) · an open
filter verb (richest, and the enumeration hazard entire).
# ''Write reach.'' `temp` alone · `temp` + `draft` · `working` as well (an agent editing
beside a human with no turn-taking).
# ''Portability.'' Emit a flat-format projection from meme canon, the way a spec carrier
renders its submission pair · or drop cross-harness portability.
# ''The pull ceiling'' — its number, and whether the frame carries it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/build-order>>

!! Build Order

Each step stands alone; none blocks the next.

# ''`render` end to end'' — one `lar:` URI returns rendered text over the socket. Nothing
else moves first.
# ''`lares kairos``'' against check set one — ruled already, and it exercises the same door.
# ''Slim the frame'' to bearing plus doors, behind the cold-floor ruling.
# ''`put`'' into the live layers, cap-gated.
# ''The flat-format projection.''

''Precondition for every step: the daemon stands.'' Each door in this design runs through it.

<<~/ahu>>

